  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Go and travel",
   "texto": [
    "For non-item destinations **nach** is used with names of cities and many countries: **Wir fahren nach Italien**. Some names carry article and use **in + acusativo**: **in die Schweiz**, **in die USA**. To say where you are, **in + dativo**: **Wir sind in Italien / in der Schweiz** is used."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Travel perfekt",
   "texto": [
    "**Fahren, fliegen** and **reisen** form the Perfekt with **sein** when they describe a displacement: **Wir sind nach Berlin gefahren**. **Besuchen** forms the Perfekt with **haben**: **Wir haben die Stadt besucht**. Learn the auxiliary along with the verb; not all verbs involving movement follow a single rule."
   ]
  },
